    {
      "id": "graph-view-owned-node-interiors-instructions",
      "type": "markdown",
      "label": "Rendering Ownership Contract",
      "root": false,
      "position": {
        "x": -220,
        "y": 700
      },
      "width": 760,
      "height": 300,
      "ports": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
          "id": "top",
          "label": "top",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 270
        },
        {
          "id": "right",
          "label": "right",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "bottom",
          "label": "bottom",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 90
        },
        {
          "id": "left",
          "label": "left",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 180
        }
      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "graph-view-owned-node-interiors"
        },
        "markdown": "## Rendering ownership\n\n**Semantic node** owns identity and state. **Graph** owns authored instances and relationships. **Graph view** owns the complete representation: content, interior, background, and semantic density. **Runtime** owns chrome, placement, focus, resize, and boundary handles.\n\nPipeline: resolve semantic node → resolve the exact exposed graph view → render its background and payload → wrap it in runtime chrome → attach boundary capabilities.\n\nA missing view is an authoring defect. Browse mode does not invent one; edit mode names the missing exposure. HTML backgrounds are sanitized and inert in this slice. Interactive document surfaces remain sandboxed capabilities.\n\nAcceptance: the same authored view renders in graph and workspace contexts, no generic gray fill sits beneath collapsed views, and no implicit Detail-to-Glyph fallback occurs."
      },
      "handles": [
        {
          "id": "root",
          "label": "root",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "any",
          "angle": 210
        },
        {
          "id": "top",
          "label": "top",
          "direction": "bidirectional",
          "dataType": "value",
          "angle": 270
        },
        {
          "id": "right",
